      "arity": {
        "min": 4,
        "max": 4,
        "variadic": false
      },
      "outputKind": "unknown",
      "outputCardinality": "unknown",
      "effect": "unknown",
      "dimension": "unknown",
      "safety": "unknown",
      "description": "Returns a list of frequencies for the corresponding Histogram Command. If Use density = false, returns the same list as Frequency( <List of Class Boundaries>, <List of Raw Data> ) If Use density = true, returns the list of frequencies of each class.",
      "usage": {
        "text": "Returns a list of frequencies for the corresponding xref:/commands/Histogram.adoc[Histogram Command].\n  If _Use density_ = _false_, returns the same list as Frequency( <List of Class Boundaries>, <List of Raw Data> )\n  If _Use density_ = _true_, returns the list of frequencies of each class.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\nLet `++data = {1, 2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 4, 4, 4, 4}++` be the list of raw data and `++classes={0, 2, 5}++` the list of class\nboundaries. Then `++Frequency(classes, data, false)++` and `++Frequency(classes, data)++` both return the list _{1,\n9}_, while `++Frequency(classes, data, true)++` returns the list _{0.5, 3}_.\n\n====",
        "truncated": false
      },
