      "safety": "unknown",
      "description": "Yields the following function: The first two numbers determine the start x-value and the end x-value. The rest of the numbers are the y-values of the function in between in equal distances.",
      "usage": {
        "text": "Yields the following function: The first two numbers determine the start _x_-value and the end _x_-value. The rest of\n  the numbers are the _y_-values of the function in between in equal distances.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n* `++Function[{2, 4, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0}]++` yields a triangular wave between _x = 2_ and _x = 4_.\n* `++Function[{-3, 3, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5}]++` yields a linear equation with slope _= 1_ between _x = -3_ and _x = 3_.\n\n====",
        "truncated": false
      },
