      "dimension": "unknown",
      "safety": "unknown",
      "description": "Yields an intersection point of two objects by using a numerical, iterative method with initial point.",
      "usage": {
        "text": "Yields an intersection point of two objects by using a numerical, iterative method with initial point.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\nLet `++a(x) = x^3 + x^2 - x++` be a function, `++b: -3x + 5y = 4++` be a line, and _C_ = (0, 0.8) be the initial point.\n`++Intersect(a, b, C)++` yields the intersection point _D_ = (-0.43, 0.54) of the function and the line by using a\nnumerical, iterative method.\n\n====",
        "truncated": false
      },
