      "outputCardinality": "unknown",
      "effect": "unknown",
      "dimension": "unknown",
      "safety": "unknown",
      "description": "Computes the inverse of the cumulative distribution function of a https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Log-normaldistributionlog-normal distribution at probability p, where the log-normal distribution is defined by the given parameters mean and standard deviation. In other words, it finds t such that P(X ≤ t) = p, where X is a log-normal random variable. Probability p must be a value in the closed interval 0, 1.",
      "usage": {
        "text": "Computes the inverse of the cumulative distribution function of a\n  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Log-normal_distribution[log-normal distribution] at probability _p_, where the log-normal\n  distribution is defined by the given parameters _mean_ and _standard deviation_.\n  In other words, it finds _t_ such that _P(X ≤ t) = p_, where _X_ is a log-normal random variable.\n  Probability _p_ must be a value in the closed interval [_0, 1_].\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n* `++InverseLogNormal(10, 20, 1/3)++` returns _3.997_.\n* `++InverseLogNormal(1000, 2, 1)++` returns stem:[ \\infty ].\n\n====",
        "truncated": false
      },
