      "safety": "unknown",
      "description": "Returns the least integer n such that P(X≤n) ≥ p, where X is a https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ZipfdistributionZipf random variable defined by the given number of elements and exponent, and p is the probability.",
      "usage": {
        "text": "Returns the least integer _n_ such that _P(X≤n) ≥ p_, where X is a https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zipf_distribution[Zipf\n  random variable] defined by the given _number of elements_ and _exponent_, and _p_ is the probability.\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nSee also xref:/commands/Zipf.adoc[Zipf Command].\n\n====",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "context": {
        "overview": {
          "text": "",
          "truncated": false
        },
        "related": [
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/Zipf.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/Zipf/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "be394ff242533bb07e66d61a73805b66cabb1999788ccf226186df07a815674d",
            "text": "= Zipf Command\n:page-en: commands/Zipf\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\nZipf( <Number of Elements>, <Exponent> )::\n  Returns a bar graph of a https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zipf%27s_law[Zipf distribution].\n  Parameters:\n  _Number of Elements_: number of elements whose rank we study\n  _Exponent_: exponent characterizing the distribution\nZipf( <Number of Elements>, <Exponent> , <Boolean Cumulative> )::\n  Returns a bar graph of a _Zipf distribution_ when _Cumulative_ = false.\n  Returns a graph of a cumulative Zipf distribution when _Cumulative_ = true.\n  First two parameters are same as above.\nZipf( <Number of Elements>, <Exponent> , <Variable Value v>, <Boolean Cumulative> )::\n  Let X be a Zipf random variable.\n  Returns P( X = _v_) when _Cumulative_ = false.\n  Returns P( X ≤ _v_) when _Cumulative_ = true.\n  First two parameters are same as above.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++Zipf(10, 1 , 5, false)++` yields _0.07_ in the image:16px-Menu_view_algebra.svg.png[Menu view\nalgebra.svg,width=16,height=16] _Algebra View_ and _stem:[\\frac{504}{7381}]_ in the\nimage:16px-Menu_view_cas.svg.png[Menu view cas.svg,width=16,height=16] _CAS View_.\n\n====\n",
            "truncated": false
          }
        ],
        "omittedRelated": 0
      },
      "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/InverseZipf.adoc",
      "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/InverseZipf/",
