      "usage": {
        "text": "Returns the Laplace transform of the function, with respect to the given variable.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++Laplace(sin(a*t),t)++` returns stem:[\\mathbf{\\frac{a}{a^{2} + t^{2}}}]\n\n`++Laplace(sin(a*t),a)++` returns stem:[\\mathbf{\\frac{t}{a^{2} + t^{2}}}]\n\n====",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "context": {
        "overview": {
          "text": "",
          "truncated": false
        },
        "related": [
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/InverseLaplace.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/InverseLaplace/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "98f22fa53589a567053d7ba8c485da1a111eda87db59729638dbf51f1cf8198e",
            "text": "= InverseLaplace Command\n:page-en: commands/InverseLaplace\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\n== CAS Syntax\n\nInverseLaplace( <Function> )::\n  Returns the https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inverse_Laplace_transform[inverse Laplace transform] of the given function.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++ InverseLaplace(1/(1+t^2))++` returns stem:[\\mathbf{ sin(t)} ].\n\n====\n\nInverseLaplace( <Function>, <Variable> )::\n  Returns the inverse Laplace transform of the function, with respect to the given variable.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++InverseLaplace( exp(- a*b),a)++` returns stem:[\\mathbf{Dirac(a-b)}]\n\n`++InverseLaplace( exp(- a*b),b)++` returns stem:[\\mathbf{Dirac(b-a)}]\n\n====\n\nInverseLaplace( <Function>, <Original Variable>, <Transformed Variable>  )::\n  Returns the inverse Laplace transform of the given function with respect to the original variable, expressed in terms of the transformed variable.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++InverseLaplace(1/(s^2+1),s,x)++` returns stem:[\\mathbf{ sin(x)}]\n\n====\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nSee also xref:/commands/Laplace.adoc[Laplace] command.\n\n====\n",
            "truncated": false
          }
        ],
        "omittedRelated": 0
      },
      "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/Laplace.adoc",
