        "related": [
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/tools/Extrude_to_Prism_or_Cylinder.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/tools/Extrude_to_Prism_or_Cylinder/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "18297c0b306b410503a1b5eaf3d508e0d6cfef3b3254e5629cae7662d8477a0d",
            "text": "= Extrude to Prism or Cylinder Tool\n:page-en: tools/Extrude_to_Prism_or_Cylinder\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\nActivate the tool, then:\n\n* Select and drag a polygon or a circle to create a right prism or cylinder.\n\nor\n\n* Select a polygon or a circle, then enter the value of the altitude in the appearing input box to create a right prism or cylinder. In Classic v.5, the checkbox \"Positive values follow the view\" is active by default and sets the positive direction of the altitude of the prism or cylinder towards the user.\n",
            "truncated": false
          },
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/tools/Prism.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/tools/Prism/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "d7e7903c875ffac6f5417fdcd3372c5f9a9f7af56da248a095d41a37c199d2b9",
            "text": "= Prism Tool\n:page-en: tools/Prism\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\nActivate the tool, select or create a polygon as bottom base, then select or create a vertex of the top base.\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\n* The vertex selected for the top base will be connected to the vertex of the bottom base that has been created or selected as first.\n\n* See also the xref:/commands/Prism.adoc[Prism] command.\n\n====\n",
            "truncated": false
          }
        ],
        "omittedRelated": 0
