      "description": "Calculates the roots for function in the given interval. The function must be continuous on that interval. Because this algorithm is numeric, it may not find all the roots in some cases.",
      "usage": {
        "text": "Calculates the roots for function in the given interval. The function must be continuous on that interval. Because\n  this algorithm is numeric, it may not find all the roots in some cases.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++Roots(f, -2, 1)++` with the function `++f(x) = 3x³ + 3x² - x++` yields\n`++A = (-1.264, 0), B = (0, 0), C = (0.264, 0)++`\n\n====\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nSee also xref:/commands/Root.adoc[Root] command\n\n====",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "context": {
        "overview": {
          "text": "",
          "truncated": false
        },
        "related": [
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/Root.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/Root/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "3a8868635fb64aafc7583e1432d5590f525827422f176994d1d26f9bfb2a79a8",
            "text": "= Root Command\n:page-en: commands/Root\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\nRoot( <Polynomial> )::\n  Yields all roots of the polynomial as intersection points of the function graph and the _x_‐axis.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++Root(0.1*x^2 - 1.5*x + 5)++` yields _A = (5, 0)_ and _B = (10, 0)_.\n\n====\n\nRoot( <Function>, <Initial x-Value> )::\n  Yields one root of the function using the initial value _a_ for a numerical iterative method.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++Root(0.1*x^2 - 1.5*x + 5, 6)++` yields _A = (5, 0)_.\n\n====\n\nRoot( <Function>, <Start x-Value>, <End x-Value> )::\n  Let _a_ be the _Start x-Value_ and _b_ the _End x-Value_ . This command yields one root of the function in the\n  interval [_a, b_] using a numerical iterative method.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++Root(0.1x² - 1.5x + 5, 8, 13)++` yields _A = (10, 0)_.\n\n====\n\n== CAS Syntax\n\nRoot( <Polynomial> )::\n  Yields all roots of the polynomial as a list.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++Root(x^3 - 3 * x^2 - 4 * x + 12)++` yields _{x = -2, x = 2, x = 3}_.\n\n====\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nIn the image:16px-Menu_view_cas.svg.png[Menu view cas.svg,width=16,height=16] xref:/CAS_View.adoc[CAS View], this\ncommand is only a special variant of xref:/commands/Solve.adoc[Solve Command].\n\n====\n",
            "truncated": false
          }
        ],
        "omittedRelated": 0
      },
      "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/Roots.adoc",
      "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/Roots/",
      "sourceCommit": "16454c25f339d10bcf99cfcbc5587b4ad19b24ba",
      "contentHash": "9d2a26cf43c8b68353279365c2963765bfb9a6750d33e9aebbf7b345b884a44d"
