      "id": "set-layer-e6c2d47adf5d",
      "command": "SetLayer",
      "signature": "SetLayer( <Object>, <Layer> )",
      "parameterTypes": [
        "object",
        "layer"
      ],
      "parameterRoles": [
        "Object",
        "Layer"
      ],
      "arity": {
        "min": 2,
        "max": 2,
        "variadic": false
      },
      "outputKind": "unknown",
      "outputCardinality": "unknown",
      "effect": "unknown",
      "dimension": "unknown",
      "safety": "unknown",
      "description": "Sets the layer for given object, where number of the layer must be an integer between 0 and 9 included.",
      "usage": {
        "text": "Sets the xref:/Layers.adoc[layer] for given object, where number of the layer must be an integer between 0 and 9 included.",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "context": {
        "overview": {
          "text": "",
          "truncated": false
        },
        "related": [
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/Layers.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/Layers/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "56d312d8d04a126866529394c9337774eb8561581548cbc4879d58cb072b745d",
            "text": "= Layers\n:page-en: Layers\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nIn GeoGebra, layers are used to determine which object to select or drag when the user clicks on multiple objects at the\nsame time.\n\n====\n\nBy default, all objects are drawn on layer 0, which is basically the background layer of the\nimage:16px-Menu_view_graphics.svg.png[Menu view graphics.svg,width=16,height=16] xref:/Graphics_View.adoc[Graphics\nView]. A total of 10 layers are available (numbers 0 to 9) and higher numbered layers are drawn on top of lower numbered\nlayers.\n\nUsing the _Advanced_ tab of the xref:/Properties_Dialog.adoc[Properties Dialog], you can change the layer for a certain\nobject (layers from 0 to 9 available). Once you change the layer number for at least one object to be different from\nlayer 0 (e.g. to layer 3), all new objects will be drawn on the layer with the highest number that is used for any\nobject - with the exception of layer 9 (so you can reserve layer 9 for objects that must always remain on top)\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nAfter selecting any object in the GeoGebra Desktop Version, you can select all objects in the same layer by selecting\nitem _Select Current Layer_ (keyboard shortcut: [.kcode]#Ctrl# + [.kcode]#L#) from the Edit menu. This menu item is only\navailable if all selected objects lie on the same layer.\n\n====\n\n== Further use of layers\n\n* For SVG export, objects are grouped by layer.\n* Layers can be controlled using the JavaScript Interface for xref:/Export_Worksheet_Dialog.adoc[GeoGebra applets].\n",
            "truncated": false
          }
        ],
        "omittedRelated": 0
      },
