        "related": [
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/First.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/First/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "1acf00ffbc8055ff6d8cfbbfd2fa8f6bd245b5426cb7dc57e4d24189dd5b44b1",
            "text": "= First Command\n:page-en: commands/First\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\nFirst( <List> )::\n  Gives a new list that contains the first element of the given list.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++First({1, 4, 3})++` yields _{1}_.\n\n====\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nTo get the first element use `++Element({1, 4, 3}, 1)++`.\n\n====\n\nFirst( <List>, <Number n of elements> )::\n\nGives a new list that contains just the first _n_ elements of the given list.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++First({1, 4, 3}, 2)++` yields _{1, 4}_.\n\n====\n\n\nFirst( <Text> )::\n  Gives first character of the text.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++First(\"Hello\")++` yields _\"H\"_.\n\n====\n\nFirst( <Text> , <Number n of elements> )::\n  Gives the first _n_ characters of the text.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++First(\"Hello\",2)++` yields _\"He\"_.\n\n====\n\nFirst( <Locus>, <Number n of elements> )::\n  This command is useful for\n  * loci generated by xref:/commands/NSolveODE.adoc[NSolveODE Command] - It returns list points that were created in the\n  first _n_ steps of the numeric ODE-solving algorithm.\n  * loci generated using xref:/commands/ShortestDistance.adoc[ShortestDistance Command],\n  xref:/commands/TravelingSalesman.adoc[TravelingSalesman Command], xref:/commands/Voronoi.adoc[Voronoi Command],\n  xref:/commands/MinimumSpanningTree.adoc[MinimumSpanningTree Command] and xref:/commands/ConvexHull.adoc[ConvexHull\n  Command] Commands - It returns vertices of the graph.\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nSee also xref:/commands/Last.adoc[Last Command].\n\n====\n",
            "truncated": false
          },
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/Length.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/Length/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "96353b8e81630818e7fe5aa44e415301a3d92603c1c3459f540c6a1b9af0161e",
            "text": "= Length Command\n:page-en: commands/Length\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\nLength( <Object> )::\n  Yields the length of the object.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n* `++Length( <Vector> )++` yields the length of the vector.\n* `++Length( <Point> )++` yields the length of the position vector of the given point.\n* `++Length( <List> )++` yields the length of the list, which is the number of elements in the list.\n* `++Length( <Text> )++` yields the number of characters in the text.\n* `++Length( <Locus> )++` returns the number of points that the given locus is made up of. Use\nxref:/commands/Perimeter.adoc[Perimeter](Locus) to get the length of the locus itself. For details see the article about\nxref:/commands/First.adoc[First Command].\n* `++Length( <Arc> )++` returns the _arc length_ (i.e. just the length of the curved section) of an arc or sector.\n\n====\n\nLength( <Function>, <Start x-Value>, <End x-Value> )::\n  Yields the length of the function graph in the given interval.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++Length(2x, 0, 1)++` returns _2.236067977_, about stem:[\\sqrt{5}].\n\n====\n\nLength( <Function>, <Start Point>, <End Point> )::\n  Yields the length of the function graph between the two points.\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nIf the given points do not lie on the function graph, their x‐coordinates are used to determine the interval.\n\n====\n\nLength( <Curve>, <Start t-Value>, <End t-Value> )::\n  Yields the length of the curve between the two values *of the parameter*.\nLength( <Curve>, <Start Point>, <End Point> )::\n  Yields the length of the curve between the two points that lie on the curve.\n\n\n\n== CAS Syntax\n\nLength( <Function>, <Start x-Value>, <End x-Value> )::\n  Calculates the length of a function graph between the two points.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++Length(2 x, 0, 1)++` yields stem:[\\sqrt{5}].\n\n====\n\nLength( <Function>, <Variable>, <Start x-Value>, <End x-Value> )::\n  Calculates the length of a function graph from _Start x-value_ to _End x-value_.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++Length(2 a, a,  0, 1)++` yields stem:[\\sqrt{5}].\n\n====\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nSee also image:22px-Mode_distance.svg.png[Mode distance.svg,width=22,height=22]\nxref:/tools/Distance_or_Length.adoc[Distance or Length] tool.\n\n====\n",
            "truncated": false
          },
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/SlopeField.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/SlopeField/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "3bd7491ea9382378d7755b65ed2e55237c911651d37a353d45909607d735d3cb",
            "text": "= SlopeField Command\n:page-en: commands/SlopeField\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\nSlopeField( <f(x,y)> )::\n  Plots a https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slope_field[slope field] of the differential equation\n  stem:[\\frac{dy}{dx}=f(x,y)]\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++SlopeField(x+y)++` plots the slope field of the differential equation stem:[\\frac{dy}{dx}=x+y]. \n\n====\n\nSlopeField( <f(x,y)>, <Number n> )::\n  Plots a slope field of the differential equation stem:[\\frac{dy}{dx}=f(x,y)] on an n by n grid (if the\n  image:16px-Menu_view_graphics.svg.png[Menu view graphics.svg,width=16,height=16] xref:/Graphics_View.adoc[Graphics\n  View] is square) or a smaller grid if not. Default is 40.\n\nSlopeField( <f(x,y)>, <Number n>, <Length Multiplier a> )::\n  Plots a slope field of the differential equation stem:[\\frac{dy}{dx}=f(x,y)]. The Length Multiplier 0<a≤1 determines\n  how long the segments are.\n\nSlopeField( <f(x,y)>, <Number n>, <Length Multiplier a>, <Min x>, <Min y>, <Max x>, <Max y> )::\n  Plots a slope field of the differential equation stem:[\\frac{dy}{dx}=f(x,y)] inside the specified rectangle (rather\n  than filling the image:16px-Menu_view_graphics.svg.png[Menu view graphics.svg,width=16,height=16]\n  xref:/Graphics_View.adoc[Graphics View])\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\n* Use the following tools: image:22px-Mode_translateview.svg.png[Mode translateview.svg,width=22,height=22]\nxref:/tools/Move_Graphics_View.adoc[Move Graphics View], image:22px-Mode_zoomin.svg.png[Mode\nzoomin.svg,width=22,height=22] xref:/tools/Zoom_In.adoc[Zoom In], image:22px-Mode_zoomout.svg.png[Mode\nzoomout.svg,width=22,height=22] xref:/tools/Zoom_Out.adoc[Zoom Out] and observe the effect.\n* See also xref:/commands/SolveODE.adoc[SolveODE], xref:/commands/Locus.adoc[Locus],\nxref:/commands/Integral.adoc[Integral]\n====\n",
            "truncated": false
          }
        ],
        "omittedRelated": 0
