      "outputCardinality": "unknown",
      "effect": "unknown",
      "dimension": "unknown",
      "safety": "unknown",
      "description": "Performs a paired t-test using the given lists of paired sample data. Tail has possible values \"<\", \">\" , \"≠\" that determine the following alternative hypotheses: + \"<\" = μ < 0 + \">\" = μ > 0 + \"≠\" = μ ≠ 0 + ( μ is the mean paired difference of the population)",
      "usage": {
        "text": "Performs a paired t-test using the given lists of paired sample data. _Tail_ has possible values \"<\", \">\" , \"≠\" that\n  determine the following alternative hypotheses: +\n  \"<\" = μ < 0 +\n  \">\" = μ > 0 +\n  \"≠\" = μ ≠ 0 +\n  ( μ is the mean paired difference of the population)\n\nResults are returned in list form as _{Probability value, t-test statistic}_.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++TTestPaired({1, 2, 3, 4, 5}, {1, 1, 3, 5, 5}, \"<\")++` yields _{0.5, 0}_.\n\n====",
        "truncated": false
      },
