      "description": "Creates a turtle at the coordinate origin.",
      "usage": {
        "text": "Creates a turtle at the coordinate origin.\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nSee also xref:/commands/TurtleForward.adoc[TurtleForward], xref:/commands/TurtleBack.adoc[TurtleBack],\nxref:/commands/TurtleLeft.adoc[TurtleLeft], xref:/commands/TurtleRight.adoc[TurtleRight],\nxref:/commands/TurtleUp.adoc[TurtleUp] and xref:/commands/TurtleDown.adoc[TurtleDown] commands.\n\n====",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "context": {
        "overview": {
          "text": "",
          "truncated": false
        },
        "related": [
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/TurtleBack.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/TurtleBack/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "6d475abc1101f0909d70ec05a9f6e3f4815776712901950e33e819e5392ffaba",
            "text": "= TurtleBack Command\n:page-en: commands/TurtleBack\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\nTurtleBack( <Turtle>, <Distance> )::\n  The turtle moves back with given distance.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\nIf the turtle is at the origin of the coordinates and the image:Animate_Pause.png[Animate Pause.png,width=16,height=16]\n_Pause_ button is displayed the command `++TurtleBack(turtle, 2)++` moves the turtle to the point (-2, 0). Otherwise you\nmust press the image:Animate_Play.png[Animate Play.png,width=16,height=16] _Play_ button so that the displacement is\neffected.\n\n====\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nSee also xref:/commands/Turtle.adoc[Turtle], xref:/commands/TurtleForward.adoc[TurtleForward],\nxref:/commands/TurtleLeft.adoc[TurtleLeft] and xref:/commands/TurtleRight.adoc[TurtleRight] commands.\n\n====\n",
            "truncated": false
          },
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/TurtleDown.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/TurtleDown/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "3893a9dcb06c16cc1d7b07743263b2e9bc0a72eae388c9e628e5dbbfaedcacf5",
            "text": "= TurtleDown Command\n:page-en: commands/TurtleDown\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\nTurtleDown( <Turtle> )::\n\nAuthorizes the turtle named to trace its movement from now.\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nSee also command xref:/commands/TurtleUp.adoc[TurtleUp]\n====\n",
            "truncated": false
          },
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/TurtleForward.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/TurtleForward/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "86ba3343eb4c667b134073a5bf531d28714033cb4361668ebe4cef96fa39a55f",
            "text": "= TurtleForward Command\n:page-en: commands/TurtleForward\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\nTurtleForward( <Turtle>, <Distance> )::\n  The turtle moves forward with given distance.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\nIf the turtle is at the origin of the coordinates and the image:Animate_Pause.png[Animate Pause.png,width=16,height=16]\n_Pause_ button is displayed the command `++TurtleForward(turtle, 2)++` moves the turtle to the point (2, 0). Otherwise\nyou must press the image:Animate_Play.png[Animate Play.png,width=16,height=16] _Play_ button so that the displacement is\neffected.\n\n====\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nSee also xref:/commands/Turtle.adoc[Turtle], xref:/commands/TurtleBack.adoc[TurtleBack],\nxref:/commands/TurtleLeft.adoc[TurtleLeft] and xref:/commands/TurtleRight.adoc[TurtleRight] commands.\n\n====\n",
            "truncated": false
          },
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/TurtleLeft.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/TurtleLeft/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "dcfa8ecc2d35a9a81eaa8454ea0f22e79a85d77d2f878396dec76256976832ed",
            "text": "= TurtleLeft Command\n:page-en: commands/TurtleLeft\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\nTurtleLeft( <Turtle>, <Angle> )::\n  The turtle turns to the left by a given angle.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++TurtleLeft(turtle, 1)++` turns the turtle to the left by 1 rad, if image:Animate_Pause.png[Animate\nPause.png,width=16,height=16] _Pause_ button is displayed. Otherwise you must press the image:Animate_Play.png[Animate\nPlay.png,width=16,height=16] _Play_ button so that the rotation is effected.\n\n====\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\nIf you enter `++TurtleLeft(turtle, 1°)++` the turtle turns to the left by 1 degree.\n\n====\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nSee also xref:/commands/Turtle.adoc[Turtle], xref:/commands/TurtleBack.adoc[TurtleBack],\nxref:/commands/TurtleForward.adoc[TurtleForward] and xref:/commands/TurtleRight.adoc[TurtleRight] commands.\n\n====\n",
            "truncated": false
          }
        ],
        "omittedRelated": 2
      },
