      "id": "upper-sum-d8d42f5b46c4",
      "command": "UpperSum",
      "signature": "UpperSum( <Function>, <Start x-Value>, <End x-Value>, <Number of Rectangles> )",
      "parameterTypes": [
        "function",
        "start x-value",
        "end x-value",
        "number of rectangles"
      ],
      "parameterRoles": [
        "Function",
        "Start x-Value",
        "End x-Value",
        "Number of Rectangles"
      ],
      "arity": {
        "min": 4,
        "max": 4,
        "variadic": false
      },
      "outputKind": "unknown",
      "outputCardinality": "unknown",
      "effect": "unknown",
      "dimension": "unknown",
      "safety": "unknown",
      "description": "Calculates the upper sum of the function on the interval Start x-Value, End x-Value using n rectangles.",
      "usage": {
        "text": "Calculates the _upper sum_ of the function on the interval [_Start x-Value, End x-Value_] using _n_ rectangles.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++UpperSum(x^2, -2, 4, 6)++` yields _35_.\n\n====\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\n* This command draws the rectangles of the upper sum as well.\n* This command is designed as a visual aid so won't give accurate answers if the number of rectangles is too large.\n* See also the commands: xref:/commands/LowerSum.adoc[LowerSum], xref:/commands/LeftSum.adoc[LeftSum],\nxref:/commands/RectangleSum.adoc[RectangleSum], and xref:/commands/TrapezoidalSum.adoc[TrapezoidalSum].\n\n====",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "context": {
        "overview": {
          "text": "",
          "truncated": false
        },
        "related": [
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/LeftSum.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/LeftSum/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "31276fb894ddfc53e1ba99a85cfb5c90572b395ee54173fce6738d1edb341b23",
            "text": "= LeftSum Command\n:page-en: commands/LeftSum\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\nLeftSum( <Function>, <Start x-Value>, <End x-Value>, <Number of Rectangles> )::\n  Calculates the left sum of the function in the interval using _n_ rectangles.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++LeftSum(x^2 + 1, 0, 2, 4)++` yields _a_ = 3.75\n\n====\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\n* This command draws the rectangles of the left sum as well.\n* This command is designed as a visual aid so won't give accurate answers if the number of rectangles is too large.\n* See also the commands: xref:/commands/RectangleSum.adoc[RectangleSum],\nxref:/commands/TrapezoidalSum.adoc[TrapezoidalSum], xref:/commands/LowerSum.adoc[LowerSum] and\nxref:/commands/UpperSum.adoc[UpperSum].\n\n====\n",
            "truncated": false
          },
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/LowerSum.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/LowerSum/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "64876d18371d67037f1564fddba85e6fa5ce572525d947341daf79025591c222",
            "text": "= LowerSum Command\n:page-en: commands/LowerSum\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\nLowerSum( <Function>, <Start x-Value>, <End x-Value>, <Number of Rectangles> )::\n  Calculates the _lower sum_ of the given function on the interval [_Start x-Value, End x-Value_], using _n_ rectangles.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++LowerSum(x^2, -2, 4, 6)++` yields _15_.\n\n====\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\n* This command draws the rectangles for the lower sum as well.\n* This command is designed as a visual aid so won't give accurate answers if the number of rectangles is too large.\n* See also the commands: xref:/commands/UpperSum.adoc[UpperSum], xref:/commands/LeftSum.adoc[LeftSum],\nxref:/commands/RectangleSum.adoc[RectangleSum], and xref:/commands/TrapezoidalSum.adoc[TrapezoidalSum].\n\n====\n",
            "truncated": false
          },
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/RectangleSum.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/RectangleSum/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "573f2e402b4edcb45182d3ee155aa617f2073dd5fcd8ea7e05bba7c0f06814ca",
            "text": "= RectangleSum Command\n:page-en: commands/RectangleSum\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\nRectangleSum( <Function>, <Start x-Value>, <End x-Value>, <Number of Rectangles>, <Position for rectangle start> )::\n  Calculates between the _Start x-Value_ and the _End x-Value_ the sum of rectangles with left height starting at a\n  fraction _d_ (0 ≤ _d_ ≤ 1) of each interval, using _n_ rectangles.\n  When _d_ = 0 it is equivalent to the xref:/commands/LeftSum.adoc[LeftSum] command, and when _d_ = 1 it computes the\n  right sum of the given function.\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\n* This command draws the rectangles of the left sum as well.\n* This command is designed as a visual aid so won't give accurate answers if the number of rectangles is too large.\n* See also the commands: xref:/commands/UpperSum.adoc[UpperSum], xref:/commands/LowerSum.adoc[LowerSum],\nxref:/commands/LeftSum.adoc[LeftSum] , xref:/commands/TrapezoidalSum.adoc[TrapezoidalSum].\n\n====\n",
            "truncated": false
          },
          {
            "sourcePath": "en/modules/ROOT/pages/commands/TrapezoidalSum.adoc",
            "sourceUrl": "https://geogebra.github.io/docs/manual/en/commands/TrapezoidalSum/",
            "available": true,
            "contentHash": "25395c2477059a648f332d4de91f6b288e1e7e4c0d09276afd0bd130a0847bd9",
            "text": "= TrapezoidalSum Command\n:page-en: commands/TrapezoidalSum\n:page-aliases: commands/TrapeziumSum.adoc\nifdef::env-github[:imagesdir: /en/modules/ROOT/assets/images]\n\n[NOTE]\n====\nimage:64px-Globe.png[Globe.png,width=64,height=64,role=left]\n\nThis command differs among variants of English:\n\n* TrapezoidalSum (US)\n* TrapeziumSum (UK + Aus)\n\n====\n\nTrapezoidalSum( <Function>, <Start x-Value>, <End x-Value>, <Number of Trapezoids> )::\n  Calculates the trapezoidal sum of the function in the interval [_Start x-Value, End x-Value_] using _n_ trapezoids.\n\n[EXAMPLE]\n====\n\n`++TrapezoidalSum(x^2, -2, 3, 5)++` yields _12.5_.\n\n====\n\n[NOTE]\n====\n\nThis command draws the trapezoids of the trapezoidal sum as well.\n* This command is designed as a visual aid so won't give accurate answers if the number of rectangles is too large.\n* See also the commands: xref:/commands/LowerSum.adoc[LowerSum], xref:/commands/LeftSum.adoc[LeftSum],\nxref:/commands/RectangleSum.adoc[RectangleSum] and xref:/commands/UpperSum.adoc[UpperSum].\n\n====\n",
            "truncated": false
          }
        ],
        "omittedRelated": 0
      },
